From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 23 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix disposal, clipping and culture defects found by review

Defects found while reviewing the solution, each covered by a new functional test.

Control
 - Dispose() was declared `new`, shadowing Component.Dispose(). It ran Dispose(true) and then
   base.Dispose(), which ran it again, so the whole child-disposal walk executed twice; and because it
   only shadowed, callers going through IDisposable or Component - container teardown and the
   components.Dispose() in generated Designer code - bypassed it and left IsDisposed false on a disposed
   control. The contract now lives in Dispose(bool) alone, guarded and idempotent.
 - Dispose(bool) ignored its `disposing` argument, so a finalizer-driven pass would touch managed
   Cairo objects; and the off-screen CreateGraphics surface was never released.

Graphics
 - Clip was an auto-property assigned once in the constructor. No SetClip/IntersectClip/ResetClip
   overload ever wrote to it, so the getter reported the full surface however much had been clipped, and
   the setter stored a region that was never pushed to Cairo - assigning a clip did nothing at all.
 - Only Replace and Intersect were honoured; Union, Exclude, Xor and Complement silently behaved like
   Intersect, because Cairo's Clip() can only narrow. Combining now happens on the Region - which
   implements the whole family - and the result is applied to Cairo in one pass.
 - SetClip(GraphicsPath) and SetClip(Graphics) flattened their argument to a bounding box.
 - FromImage published a blank surface as the image's pixbuf, so merely asking an image for a Graphics
   erased everything already drawn on it. It now seeds the surface from the existing content.
 - The Cairo context was a public mutable field on the shipped API surface; it is internal now.

ResourceManager / ComponentResourceManager
 - The culture-taking overloads discarded their culture and read the neutral resource, so a localized
   resource could never be reached. They now walk the standard fallback chain (it-IT, it, neutral),
   looking in culture-qualified embedded resources and satellite assemblies.
 - ComponentResourceManager did not forward GetString(name, culture) at all.
 - The Content/System.ComponentModel.cs shim carried two `new` GetObject overloads that only applied
   when the static type was exactly that class, one of which dropped its culture. The base class
   overrides both correctly, so they are gone.

